{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791297657165,"sessionID":"ses_eee590d8dffeySv5wewGeCf7jF","part":{"id":"prt_111a9194b001NHxud3veP81Nwi","messageID":"msg_111a8f779001RI2xWFBlz9aZKS","sessionID":"ses_eee590d8dffeySv5wewGeCf7jF","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791297663492,"sessionID":"ses_eee590d8dffeySv5wewGeCf7jF","part":{"id":"prt_111a92103001JlNmcbjYDnErlu","messageID":"msg_111a8f779001RI2xWFBlz9aZKS","sessionID":"ses_eee590d8dffeySv5wewGeCf7jF","type":"text","text":"All 6 tests pass. I fixed 3 bugs:\n\n1. **`money.py` — `format_cents`**: negative values broke because Python floor-division on negatives gave wrong digits (`-$-4.90` for -310). Now it formats `abs(cents)` with the sign prefix, so -310 gives `-$3.10` and -5 gives `-$0.05` as documented.\n\n2. **`parse.py` — `parse_date`**: it returned `(year, day, month)`. It now returns `(year, month, day)` per the docstring. This also fixed `parse_record`.\n\n3. **`report.py` — `top_items`**: it sorted by total ascending and ignored the tie rule. It now sorts by total descending with ties broken by item name ascending, as the docstring states.\n\nNo changes to `run_tests.py`, no new files, no installs.","time":{"start":1791297659140,"end":1791297663480}}}
